 "comment": "The lower floor of the hanging cells (D-1333, D-1340, D-1354). The stair up ends on the landing. Jailers walk the hanging yard, whose chest holds the yard key, rats walk the cell rows, and the low cell holds the stump of a waystone that the church walled in, a save point (D-1339). A jailer and a hound hold the rack room. The yard door takes the yard key, and the aisle behind it leads to the cell block, where the cell watch walks in front of the cell of Dagvar. The tile in front of his bars plays his join one time, and he shows inside the closed cell (D-1337, D-1343). The cells are night and dark, so each patrol sees 2 tiles (D-1063, D-1338).",
